# Line endings: LF in the repository AND in every checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says.
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true, which checks text files out with CRLF.
# The shared contract vectors are compared byte for byte across faces (devtools
# `vector-drift` digests them), and vocabulary.ttl is served live at
# https://ikigai-rs.dev/ns, so a CRLF checkout of either is drift. `eol=lf` on a path
# overrides core.autocrlf for it. Ledger #1205.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Named explicitly, so content detection can never decide them.
crates/ikigai-vocab/tests/vectors/*.json text eol=lf
*.ttl    text eol=lf
*.jsonld text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf
